WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:20.269
"Nail," said Dad. Joy reached into her sack.

2
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.423
"Nail!" she said, handing him one.

3
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:27.373
Dad pounded it into a board with his hammer.

4
00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:30.338
"Good job!" said Joy.

5
00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:34.204
Joy and her dad had been busy all morning.

6
00:00:34.205 --> 00:00:38.814
They had moved Grandpa's wood up to the elm trees.

7
00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:43.509
Then they bought more wooden boards and posts at the lumberyard.

8
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.925
Dad put two posts in the ground and built a frame for the tree house floor.

9
00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:53.434
When he was finished, he looked at Joy with a frown.

10
00:00:53.435 --> 00:00:57.526
"Partner," he said, "we have a problem."

11
00:00:57.527 --> 00:01:01.506
"What's wrong?" asked Joy with surprise.

12
00:01:01.507 --> 00:01:07.778
"See this wood we bought for the floor?" said Dad, pointing at a pile of 12 boards.

13
00:01:07.779 --> 00:01:10.458
"They are two and a half meters long."

14
00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:15.436
Joy looked at the boards and then looked up at the frame Dad had built.

15
00:01:15.437 --> 00:01:19.274
She tilted her head and narrowed her eyes.

16
00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:21.057
Then she smiled.

17
00:01:21.058 --> 00:01:24.235
"Those boards look too long."

18
00:01:24.236 --> 00:01:28.016
"You've got a good set of eyes!" said Dad.

19
00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:33.708
"The frame is two meters long, so we need to shorten each board by half a meter."

20
00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:37.595
Dad and Joy knelt by one board.

21
00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:42.877
"Hold this tape measure at the end of the board," Dad said, handing her the measure.

22
00:01:42.878 --> 00:01:45.989
Then he pulled the tape along the edge.

23
00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.795
"That's 25 centimeters," said Joy.

24
00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:51.992
Dad pulled the tape some more.

25
00:01:51.993 --> 00:01:55.333
"And that's 50!"

26
00:01:55.334 --> 00:02:00.452
"Now I mark it with a pencil," explained Dad as he drew a black line.

27
00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.941
"That's where we will cut the board."

28
00:02:02.942 --> 00:02:07.060
"Should we measure and mark all of them?" asked Joy.

29
00:02:07.061 --> 00:02:09.041
"Yes," said Dad.

30
00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:12.203
"Then I'll cut them down to the right size.

31
00:02:12.204 --> 00:02:13.355
And you know what?

32
00:02:13.356 --> 00:02:17.127
We can take the leftover wood to the recycling center."

33
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:20.771
"Somebody else will be able to use it," said Joy.

34
00:02:20.772 --> 00:02:23.942
"Just like we used Grandpa's wood."

35
00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:29.889
By late afternoon Dad had finished nailing the tree house floor to the frame.

36
00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:35.797
He and Joy sat on the back end of the truck and looked up at their work.

37
00:02:35.798 --> 00:02:38.763
"What's next?" asked Joy.

38
00:02:38.764 --> 00:02:40.842
"Let's recycle that extra wood.

39
00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:44.943
We might find a few things we need too," said Dad.

40
00:02:44.944 --> 00:02:49.579
They got in the truck and drove down the hill to the road.

41
00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.932
When they reached the center, Joy hopped out of the truck.

42
00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:59.830
She liked looking up at the mountains of crushed cardboard and smashed soda cans.

43
00:02:59.831 --> 00:03:03.604
She saw Mr. Ramirez, Carlos' father.

44
00:03:03.605 --> 00:03:10.558
He was in charge of sorting all the metal—brass, tin, iron, steel, and copper.

45
00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:14.159
"Hello, Mr. Ramirez," called Joy.

46
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.587
"Dad and I are building a tree house!

47
00:03:16.588 --> 00:03:19.270
Do you have anything we can use?"

48
00:03:19.271 --> 00:03:22.816
"Well, let's see," said Mr. Ramirez.

49
00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:24.681
"Do you need a bucket?"

50
00:03:24.682 --> 00:03:29.158
"We might," replied Joy. "Thanks!"

51
00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:31.954
Dad was looking in a cardboard box.

52
00:03:31.955 --> 00:03:35.224
"Here are some old hooks," he said.

53
00:03:35.225 --> 00:03:39.796
"The kids can hang stuff on those," said Mr. Ramirez.

54
00:03:39.797 --> 00:03:43.453
Joy dropped the hooks into her bucket.

55
00:03:43.454 --> 00:03:47.691
"What's this?" asked Joy. "A wheel?"

56
00:03:47.692 --> 00:03:52.007
"It's a special kind of wheel," said Mr. Ramirez.

57
00:03:52.008 --> 00:03:53.709
"It's called a pulley.

58
00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:57.019
You use it with a rope to help lift something."

59
00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.990
Joy turned to her dad.

60
00:03:58.991 --> 00:04:01.076
"Do we need one?"

61
00:04:01.077 --> 00:04:06.035
"Take it," he said. "We can use it."

62
00:04:06.036 --> 00:04:09.210
"Let's take this pole too," said Joy.

63
00:04:09.211 --> 00:04:11.760
"It might be good for something."

64
00:04:11.761 --> 00:04:16.231
Then Dad found some sheets of tin leaning against a wall.

65
00:04:16.232 --> 00:04:20.439
"Our tree house roof!" cried Joy.

66
00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.064
And that wasn't all.

67
00:04:22.065 --> 00:04:26.691
They also found a small window frame and an old door.

68
00:04:26.692 --> 00:04:33.046
They piled everything in the back of the truck and drove home.
